Chapter: BoundedReturnTrap

 Bounded signatures, stage B (postcondition): an out-of-range result
 traps before the return. clamp-ret's declared return is bounded
 0..15, but its body passes through the plain-Integer parameter 99;
 the return guard traps (UD2) because 99 does not inhabit 0..15.

Section: Definitions

  clamp-ret : Integer -> Integer between 0 and 15
  clamp-ret (n) = n

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (clamp-ret 99))
  end
